    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipNumber` assignment formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, where `YY` is the last two digits of the `registrationDate` year.\n\nSince `membershipNumber` is derived purely from the owner's existing `customerCode` and `registrationDate` fields, I followed the repo's existing pattern for computed DTO fields (`initials`, `householdId`, `displayName`) rather than persisting a new column:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `membershipNumber` property to the `Owner` schema (the DTO is generated from this spec at build time).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping` expression and a `membershipNumber(owner)` helper that formats `\"%s-M%02d\"` from `customerCode` and `registrationDate.getYear() % 100`, returning `null` if either source field is absent.\n\nThe result is seed-independent and consistent with how `customerCode`, `registrationDate`, and the other derived fields already flow through the single `POST /api/owners` \u2192 `GET /api/owners/{id}` path exercised by the acceptance test.",
